(7736077, 1275212, 122678, '<td valign="top">Congratulations<br/>Certainly very New England, well presented.</td>', 'CongratulationsCertainly very New England, well presented.', '2023-01-04 07:32:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736078, 1275231, 122678, '<td valign="top">Congratulations<br/>I went back to look at this one again and again. Beautiful lights and sunset, stunning water color.</td>', 'CongratulationsI went back to look at this one again and again. Beautiful lights and sunset, stunning water color.', '2023-01-04 07:34:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736079, 1275126, 122678, '<td valign="top">Congrats<br/>Wow a beautiful spot and nice Christmas lights. I love the star effect with the lights on the bridge.</td>', 'CongratsWow a beautiful spot and nice Christmas lights. I love the star effect with the lights on the bridge.', '2023-01-04 07:38:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736087, 1275245, 122678, '<td valign="top">Congrats on this simple and elegant image.</td>', 'Congrats on this simple and elegant image.', '2023-01-04 11:39:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736088, 1275126, 122678, '<td valign="top">I keep going back to your image. It is beyond beautiful and special. There are so many beautiful effects and colors in this image. This image is stunningly beautiful. I love the crop if it is cropped, you covered the water fall and the depth of the bridge. My favorite of the challenge by far.</td>', 'I keep going back to your image. It is beyond beautiful and special. There are so many beautiful effects and colors in this image. This image is stunningly beautiful. I love the crop if it is cropped, you covered the water fall and the depth of the bridge. My favorite of the challenge by far.', '2023-01-04 11:44:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736091, 1275250, 30214, '<td valign="top">well done Mark! How many ribbons did your drone win for you this year? ))</td>', 'well done Mark! How many ribbons did your drone win for you this year? ))', '2023-01-04 14:34:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736092, 1275212, 30214, '<td valign="top">Congrats Robert! Amazing how a phone camera can handle such a complicated lighting situation</td>', 'Congrats Robert! Amazing how a phone camera can handle such a complicated lighting situation', '2023-01-04 14:35:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7736094, 1275126, 29535, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Barroness:</b></div><hr/><i> I keep going back to your image. It is beyond beautiful and special. There are so many beautiful effects and colors in this image. This image is stunningly beautiful. I love the crop if it is cropped, you covered the water fall and the depth of the bridge. My favorite of the challenge by far. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you! It really looked incredible and whilst it was a difficult capture I''m really happy with how it turned out. It was very close to a ribbon and even though it didn''t quite make it it''s one of my most magical photos that I''m very proud of. Thank you!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> thanks for the story.. I always love reading them .. <br/>your have a great writing style btw ... <br/>congratulations on getting out of your comfort zone and getting an excellent photo to boot .. <br/>and of course 4th place .. :)<br/> <br/>ps .. I love knowing the origins of sayings  .. and to boot was screaming out to be googled .. <br/> <br/>"The saying to boot comes from an Old English word bot, meaning advantage or remedy. It''s related to the contemporary English words better and best, so if something''s to boot, it''s added or extra." </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you Roz! And thanks for the trivia :D I''ll have to remember that as I''m an English teacher and those kind of questions come up all the time and I never know the answers.</td>', 'Originally posted by Barroness: I keep going back to your image. It is beyond beautiful and special. There are so many beautiful effects and colors in this image. This image is stunningly beautiful. I love the crop if it is cropped, you covered the water fall and the depth of the bridge. My favorite of the challenge by far.   Thank you! It really looked incredible and whilst it was a difficult capture I''m really happy with how it turned out. It was very close to a ribbon and even though it didn''t quite make it it''s one of my most magical photos that I''m very proud of. Thank you! Originally posted by roz: thanks for the story.. I always love reading them .. your have a great writing style btw ... congratulations on getting out of your comfort zone and getting an excellent photo to boot .. and of course 4th place .. :) ps .. I love knowing the origins of sayings  .. and to boot was screaming out to be googled ..  "The saying to boot comes from an Old English word bot, meaning advantage or remedy. It''s related to the contemporary English words better and best, so if something''s to boot, it''s added or extra."   Thank you Roz! And thanks for the trivia :D I''ll have to remember that as I''m an English teacher and those kind of questions come up all the time and I never know the answers.', '2023-01-04 16:15:28.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
